) VALUES
('ev-ubay-ubay-festival', 'Ubay-Ubay Festival', 'Culture', 'January 29', 'Jan 29', 'jan', 'Ubay', '10.0530, 124.4744', 'Annual', 'Ubay''s street-dance festival in honor of the Sto. Niño, the town''s patron. The name plays on the local etymology - ''ubay-ubay'' is Cebuano for ''alongside.'' Ubay gained separate pueblo status on January 15, 1844 and became an independent parish in 1877; the festival is the contemporary cultural showcase tied to that long Sto. Niño devotion.', 'Northeast Bohol''s biggest fiesta. If you''re coming from Tagbilaran, leave by 5am-it''s a 2.5-hour drive and parking fills early.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, ubay, sto nino, january, northeast, streetdance', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-01-29'),
('ev-kasadyaan-sa-napo', 'Kasadyaan sa Napo', 'Heritage', 'First Sunday of February', '1st Sun Feb', 'feb', 'Loon', '9.7965, 123.7964', 'Annual', 'A mid-2000s addition to Barangay Napo''s Holy Cross devotion in Loon, serving as prelude to the May 25 barangay fiesta. Street-dance contingents compete across the five traditional household clusters of Napo - Inang-angan, Kabaybayunan, Tulay, Wawog, and Tubig-Loon - followed by tableau performances and a culminating Sinulog to the Sto. Niño.', 'Smaller, more intimate than Loon''s Sept fiesta. Locals say this is the one with the real food and the real community.', NULL, NULL, 'heritage, fiesta, loon, napo, holy cross, february, barangay', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-02-01'),
('ev-pandayan-festival', 'Pandayan Festival', 'Heritage', 'February 27', 'Feb 27', 'feb', 'Jagna', '9.6483, 124.3603', 'Annual', 'First celebrated February 27, 2008, marking the 9th anniversary of St. Joseph the Worker Parish in Barangay Lonoy, Jagna. ''Pandayan'' is Cebuano for blacksmith shop - and since St. Joseph is patron of workers, the festival honors local artisans and tradespeople. Programming centers on a Carpentry and Handicrafts Fair, a 9-day novena, image procession, and street dancing.', 'Watch a live blacksmithing demo-they fire up the panday on festival day. Few places in the province still do this.', NULL, NULL, 'heritage, fiesta, jagna, lonoy, blacksmith, panday, february, craft', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-02-27'),
('ev-pana-ad-sa-loboc', 'Pana-ad sa Loboc', 'Heritage', 'Holy Thursday & Good Friday (movable)', 'Holy Week', 'hol', 'Loboc', '9.6383, 124.0357', 'Movable', 'A centuries-old folk-Catholic vow tradition rather than a programmed civic festival. ''Pana-ad'' is Cebuano for vow - pilgrims walk the Stations of the Cross on foot toward Cruz Daku, an 80-foot cross atop Loboc''s highest hill, in fulfillment of promises made for healing or thanksgiving. The Pasyon is chanted throughout; the procession runs Holy Thursday and Good Friday.', 'Dress modestly. This is not a tourist event-the town treats it as devotional and visitors are welcome but expected to observe quietly.', NULL, NULL, 'heritage, devotional, loboc, holy week, procession, movable, religious, pasyon', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-03-01'),
('ev-calamay-festival', 'Calamay Festival', 'Food', 'April 27 - 28', 'Apr 27-28', 'apr', 'Jagna', '9.6520, 124.3633', 'Annual', 'Jagna''s tribute to a 190-year-old confectionery tradition organized by the LGU around the slow-cooked coconut-and-sticky-rice sweet introduced in the mid-1800s by Augustinian Recollect parish priest Fr. Mariano Gutierrez in Barangay Can-upao. Calamay is still cooked over open fire for up to seven hours in giant kawa (woks), then packaged in halved coconut shells sealed with red crepe paper. The festival pairs cooking demos with the Hudyaka sa Calamay street dance.', 'Buy calamay straight from the makers at the festival-not the highway stalls. Different recipe, fresher, half the price.', NULL, NULL, 'food, fiesta, jagna, calamay, pasalubong, coconut, april, sweet, recollect', '#fe6a36', 'rgba(254,106,54,0.12)', '#c23d10', 0, '2026-04-27'),
('ev-saulog-tagbilaran', 'Saulog Tagbilaran', 'Culture', 'May 1', 'May 1', 'may', 'Tagbilaran City', '9.6471, 123.8556', 'Annual', 'Tagbilaran''s signature festival on the feast of St. Joseph the Worker, formalized in 2013 under Mayor Baba Yap as an expansion of the long-standing patronal fiesta. ''Saulog'' is Cebuano for ''to celebrate.'' The May 1 program blends street dancing, dragon boat racing on Tagbilaran Bay, and food fairs alongside the religious feast. Resumed in 2023 after a three-year pandemic hiatus.', 'Street dance happens midday under brutal sun. Stake a shaded spot along CPG Avenue early, or come for the evening showdown finale instead.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, streetdance, tagbilaran, san jose, may, charter day, dragon boat', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-05-01'),
('ev-enting-enting-festival', 'Enting-enting Festival', 'Culture', 'May 3 - 5', 'May 3-5', 'may', 'Maribojoc', '9.7378, 123.8442', 'Annual', 'Maribojoc''s festival of miracles, tagged ''Enting-enting Basaw''g Sajaw: Parada sa mga Milagro.'' Street-dance contingents reenact the miracles attributed to San Vicente Ferrer - the town''s secondary patron - often using indigenous bamboo drums. Maribojoc Church was canonically established as a Diocesan Shrine of San Vicente Ferrer in 2005; the festival runs alongside the Holy Cross patronal feast on May 3.', 'Pair with a stop at the Punta Cruz watchtower (1796) while you''re in town-it''s the best sunset spot on the west coast.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, maribojoc, san vicente ferrer, sta cruz, may, west coast, streetdance, miracles', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-05-03'),
('ev-tanda-festival', 'Tanda Festival', 'Culture', 'May 6 - 15', 'May 6-15', 'may', 'Tubigon', '9.9520, 123.9669', 'Annual', 'Tubigon''s homecoming-themed festival in honor of San Isidro Labrador. ''Tanda'' is Cebuano for a brief visit to one''s place of origin - the festival is themed around balikbayan return. The signature element is the Bulong-Imang street dance, named for the drum-and-gong rhythm and performed as a thanksgiving dance to San Isidro Labrador, alongside the Anyag sa Tubigon pageant and an agro-tech fair.', 'Catch the weaving demo if you''re at all curious about Tubigon raffia-the town''s quiet export to Manila design shops.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, tubigon, weaving, raffia, may, coastal, port, san isidro labrador', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-05-06'),
('ev-bolibong-kingking-festival', 'Bolibong Kingking Festival', 'Music', 'May 23 - 24', 'May 23-24', 'may', 'Loboc', '9.6383, 124.0357', 'Annual', 'A healing ritual-dance traced back to 1843 at Loboc Church, performed before the image of Our Lady of Guadalupe de Extremadura - Loboc parish is also the Diocesan Shrine of that devotion. Devotees sway aching body parts to the rhythm of the bolibong (drum) and kingking (gong); the name is onomatopoeic. Local tradition attributes its origin to a 19th-century cholera outbreak when devotees prayed for healing through the Virgin''s intercession.', 'The acoustics in front of the Loboc Church are unreal. Arrive at sunset-golden light hits the church facade just as the brass starts.', NULL, NULL, 'music, fiesta, heritage, loboc, church, brass, choir, devotional, may, guadalupe, healing', '#f7d87d', 'rgba(247,216,125,0.22)', '#654b30', 0, '2026-05-23'),
('ev-sinugboan-festival', 'Sinugboan Festival', 'Culture', 'May 27', 'May 27', 'may', 'Garcia Hernandez', '9.6189, 124.2389', 'Annual', 'Garcia Hernandez''s town foundation day festival on May 27 - the date the pueblo was formally established in 1854. ''Sinugboan'' is the past-tense form of the Cebuano ''sugbo'' (to wallow or wade), signaling an event of historical weight; the festival''s street-dance storyline reenacts the founding and establishment of the town itself, including the gratitude story behind its name (in honor of Recollect priests José García of Loon and Narciso Hernández of Guindulman).', 'Smaller crowd than the big-name fiestas. Better food, fewer tourists, more local color.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, garcia hernandez, may, coastal, streetdance, foundation day', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-05-27'),
('ev-katigbawan-festival', 'Katigbawan Festival', 'Culture', 'June 17 - 24', 'Jun 17-24', 'jun', 'Catigbian', '9.8333, 124.0833', 'Annual', 'Catigbian''s week-long festival anchored on the town''s June 17, 1949 Foundation Day, when President Quirino re-established the municipality. The name fuses three roots - ''Katigbi'' (a native grass that gave the town its name), ''Tigbaw'' (Visayan for caves), and ''Kabawan'' (the carabao auction market the town is known for). Programming centers on carabao racing, a ''Miss Katigbawan'' carabao pageant, agro-fair, and hog-catching contests.', 'June 24 is the climax-street dance morning, procession evening. Earlier days are warmups and trade fair.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, catigbian, inland, june, streetdance, carabao, foundation day', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-06-17'),
('ev-agbunan-festival', 'Agbunan Festival', 'Heritage', 'June 28', 'Jun 28', 'jun', 'San Isidro', '9.9119, 124.0428', 'Annual', 'San Isidro''s town foundation day festival, first held June 28, 2009 on the municipality''s 40th Foundation Day. ''Agbunan'' was the town''s older place name - rooted in ''bugang,'' a plant whose flowers scatter (agbun) in the wind. The festival''s theme of ''Tinubdan sa Lungsoranong Kahiusahan ug Kalambuan'' frames its street dance around love for nature, agriculture, and environmental awareness.', 'Off most tourists'' radar. Go if you want to see a Bohol fiesta without any of the festival-circuit polish.', NULL, NULL, 'heritage, fiesta, san isidro, june, inland, farming, foundation day, environmental', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-06-28'),
('ev-sandugo-festival', 'Sandugo Festival', 'Culture', 'July 1 - 31 (peak around July 22)', 'Jul 1-31', 'jul', 'Tagbilaran City', '9.6499, 123.8590', 'Annual', 'Bohol''s flagship civic festival, first staged in 1989 under Governor Constancio Torralba and now organized by the Bohol Sandugo Foundation alongside the Tagbilaran City Charter Day. It commemorates the blood compact sworn between Datu Sikatuna and Miguel López de Legazpi on March 16, 1565 - called the ''first treaty of friendship'' between Filipinos and Spaniards. The month builds toward the Sandugo Street Dancing Competition and the historic re-enactment at the Blood Compact Shrine in Bool, alongside the Miss Bohol Sandugo pageant and a province-wide agro-industrial fair.', 'The Blood Compact re-enactment around July 22 is the soul of it. Skip the fair days-come for that.', NULL, 'Visit website', 'fiesta, heritage, province-wide, sandugo, blood compact, parade, streetdance, tagbilaran', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 1, '2026-07-01'),
('ev-tigum-bol-anon-tibuok-kalibutan-tbtk', 'Tigum Bol-anon Tibuok Kalibutan (TBTK)', 'Culture', 'July (every 4 years, with Sandugo)', 'Jul (every 4 yrs)', 'jul', 'Tagbilaran City', '9.6499, 123.8590', 'Quadrennial', 'A worldwide homecoming gathering of Boholanos, anchored by the provincial Capitol since the late 1990s and held every four years in conjunction with the Sandugo Celebration. The name translates as ''Gathering of Boholanos from Around the World.'' Programming centers on cultural immersions for diaspora children, civic forums, and investment pitches showcasing Bohol businesses to balikbayan capital. The pandemic interrupted the four-year cycle.', 'If you''re Boholano abroad or have family who is, this is the one to plan around. Book flights 4+ months ahead.', NULL, NULL, 'homecoming, culture, OFW, diaspora, capitol, tagbilaran, province-wide, quadrennial', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-07-04'),
('ev-panagat-sa-dauis-festival', 'Panagat sa Dauis Festival', 'Culture', 'August 14', 'Aug 14', 'aug', 'Dauis', '9.6164, 123.8595', 'Annual', 'First held in 2017 as part of Dauis''s 297th founding anniversary. ''Panagat'' combines ''pa-'' with ''dagat'' (sea) - a tribute to fishing as the town''s primary livelihood. The dance showdown features contingents in costumes inspired by sea creatures, paying homage to local fisherfolk on the eve of the patronal feast of Our Lady of the Assumption (Aug 15).', 'The fluvial parade leaves from the Dauis Church seawall at high tide. Check tide tables before you set out.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, dauis, panglao, fluvial, maritime, august, coastal, fisherfolk', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-08-14'),
('ev-hudyaka-sa-panglao', 'Hudyaka sa Panglao', 'Culture', 'August 28', 'Aug 28', 'aug', 'Panglao', '9.5784, 123.7560', 'Annual', 'A barangay-based festival started in 1985 around the feast of San Agustin, Panglao''s patron - among Bohol''s oldest community-driven festival formats. ''Hudyaka'' is Cebuano for merrymaking. Ten Panglao barangays compete on the San Agustin Church festival grounds with street dancing and choreography rooted in the town''s coastal identity, alongside the patronal mass and 9-day novena.', 'The action is at the church plaza, not Alona Beach. Locals will tell you the real fiesta is in the town proper.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, panglao, san agustin, august, streetdance, beach, barangay', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-08-28'),
('ev-sidlakasilak-festival-of-lights-of-loon', 'SidlaKasilak (Festival of Lights of Loon)', 'Culture', 'August 30 - September 8', 'Aug 30-Sep 8', 'aug', 'Loon', '9.7965, 123.7964', 'Annual', 'Loon''s 10-day festival of lights, started in 2000 to honor Birhen sa Kasilak (Our Lady of Light), the town''s patroness. The only evening street-dancing festival in the province - dancers carry illuminated props rooted in older ''parow'' lantern processions (originally candles in Japanese paper lanterns, now LEDs and magic sticks). It culminates September 8 in a fluvial procession with lit bancas on Loon Bay.', 'Go on the closing night (Sept 8). The fluvial procession at dusk-with lit candles on bancas-is what people drive across the island for.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, lights, loon, birhen sa kasilak, fluvial, devotional, september, west coast, evening', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-08-30'),
('ev-sinu-og-estokada-festival', 'Sinu-og Estokada Festival', 'Culture', 'September 29', 'Sep 29', 'sep', 'Jagna', '9.6520, 124.3633', 'Annual', 'Jagna''s heritage festival, first performed as school programs on September 29, 2001 to preserve an older ''sinu-og'' tradition tied to the patronal feast of San Miguel Arcangel. Two rival contingents from Brgy. Mayana and Brgy. Cabungaan perform a native war dance with bladed instruments (''estokada'' = fencing), reenacting historic skirmishes between early Christian Jagnaanons and Muslim raiders from Mindanao - symbolically the celestial battle of good versus evil.', 'The sword choreography is the whole point. Get close to the front-the costuming and footwork is detail you''ll miss from a distance.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, culture, jagna, san miguel, sword, september, streetdance, theatrical, estokada', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-09-29'),
('ev-ubi-festival', 'Ubi Festival', 'Harvest', 'Second week of January (recent: early December)', 'Jan / Dec', 'jan', 'Tagbilaran City', '9.6471, 123.8556', 'Annual', 'Launched by the provincial government around 2000 to honor a root crop venerated in Bohol for nearly 500 years. Ubi (purple yam) is the so-called ''savior crop'' - tradition holds it carried Boholanos through pre-Hispanic droughts. The festival showcases native varieties (kinampay, tam-isan, baligonhon, apali, iniling, kabus-ok) through cooking demos, peeling contests, and farmer recognition. Recent editions have moved from January to early December to align with the harvest window.', 'The cook-off is where it gets real. Skip the opening parade, come for the kalamay and ubi kinilaw tasting.', NULL, 'Visit website', 'harvest, food, heritage, ubi, purple yam, kinampay, agriculture, tagbilaran, province-wide', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-01-01'),
('ev-sambat-mascara-y-regatta-festival', 'Sambat Mascara y Regatta Festival', 'Culture', 'First Saturday of December', '1st Sat Dec', 'dec', 'Loay', '9.5972, 124.0179', 'Annual', 'Loay''s three-part festival in honor of St. Francis Xavier, the town''s secondary patron whose devotion in Bohol dates to 1621. The ''mascara'' element evokes the pintados - the tattooed pre-colonial Visayans - through masked street dancers. A drum-and-bugle competition runs alongside a river regatta, with the saint''s image leading a fluvial parade along the Loboc River mouth where it meets the sea.', 'The regatta starts at low tide-usually mid-morning. The riverbank past the bridge is the unblocked viewing spot.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, regatta, masked, loay, december, river, coastal, streetdance, pintados, francis xavier', '#9096ea', 'rgba(144,150,234,0.15)', '#3d3fa8', 0, '2026-12-01'),
('ev-suroy-sa-musikero', 'Suroy sa Musikero', 'Music', 'December 25 - February 2', 'Dec-Feb', 'feb', 'Loboc (and other towns)', '9.6383, 124.0357', 'Annual (seasonal)', 'A long-standing Loboc Christmas tradition - not a programmed festival - where the parish brass band goes house-to-house playing carols, songs of thanksgiving, and a ''responso'' (prayer for the dead) for each host family. The full ensemble (clarinets, trumpets, percussion, bass horns, trombones, cymbals) is what cemented Loboc''s reputation as the music town of Bohol. The season closes on February 2, the Feast of the Presentation (Candelaria).', 'You don''t go to it-it comes to you. Ask your homestay host the night before; they''ll know who''s passing through.', NULL, NULL, 'music, heritage, roving, christmas, candlemas, loboc, brass band, december, january, february', '#f7d87d', 'rgba(247,216,125,0.22)', '#654b30', 0, '2026-02-01'),
('ev-cortes-town-fiesta-sto-nino', 'Cortes Town Fiesta (Sto. Niño)', 'Heritage', 'January 16', 'Jan 16', 'jan', 'Cortes', '9.6833, 123.8833', 'Annual', 'Cortes''s patronal feast at a parish made independent in 1793-94 under the Augustinian Recollects, with the present cliff-top coral-stone church begun in 1880 above the Abatan River delta. The cruciform cut-coral building was declared a National Cultural Treasure in 2013. The town - named after Spanish conquistador Hernán Cortés - is the closest fiesta-day add-on from Tagbilaran.', 'Closest town to Tagbilaran-easy add-on. Sto. Niño procession leaves the church at 4pm.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, cortes, sto nino, january, devotional, near tagbilaran, national cultural treasure', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-01-16'),
('ev-valencia-town-fiesta-sto-nino', 'Valencia Town Fiesta (Sto. Niño)', 'Heritage', 'January 16', 'Jan 16', 'jan', 'Valencia', '9.6000, 124.2167', 'Annual', 'Valencia''s patronal feast for the Holy Infant, at a parish established in 1871 with the church built 1870-1882. Distinctive for its cruciform plan, steep roof with pyramidal crossing tower, and a wooden floor of alternating dark (tindalo/balayong) and light (molave/tugas) planks. The church is a declared National Cultural Treasure; the town was carved out of Dimiao in 1869.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, valencia, sto nino, january, south coast, devotional, national cultural treasure', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-01-16'),
('ev-pres-carlos-p-garcia-town-fiesta-sto-nino', 'Pres. Carlos P. Garcia Town Fiesta (Sto. Niño)', 'Heritage', 'January 16', 'Jan 16', 'jan', 'Pres. Carlos P. Garcia', '10.0167, 124.6167', 'Annual', 'Lapinig Island municipality''s patronal feast for the Holy Infant. The town - formerly ''Pitogo'' - was created on June 21, 1969 and renamed in 1977 for President Carlos P. Garcia, the only Boholano to serve as Philippine president. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', 'Lapinig Island fiesta-plan boat from Talibon or Ubay. Not a same-day trip.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, lapinig, sto nino, january, island, devotional, cpg', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-01-16'),
('ev-carmen-town-fiesta-san-antonio-abad', 'Carmen Town Fiesta (San Antonio Abad)', 'Heritage', 'January 17', 'Jan 17', 'jan', 'Carmen', '9.8181, 124.1819', 'Annual', 'Carmen''s patronal feast for St. Anthony the Abbot at a parish erected September 9, 1874 under the Augustinian Recollects, with stone-church construction begun in 1887. Bilar was the mother parish. Carved out of Bilar in 1868, the town is best known today as the gateway to the Chocolate Hills. Remnants of Spanish-era coral stone survive at the facade base; most of the present fabric is 1920s.', 'Carmen fiesta pairs best with a Chocolate Hills sunrise the next morning-stay overnight in town.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, carmen, san antonio abad, january, chocolate hills, devotional', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-01-17'),
('ev-ubay-town-fiesta-sto-nino', 'Ubay Town Fiesta (Sto. Niño)', 'Heritage', 'January 29', 'Jan 29', 'jan', 'Ubay', '10.0530, 124.4744', 'Annual', 'Ubay''s patronal feast at the parish declared in 1877 with first Recollect priest Fr. Blas Adan del Pilar. The colonial-era wooden church was replaced by a concrete church, which was itself destroyed by Typhoon Ining in 1968; the present church was built on the earlier footprint. Bohol''s largest municipality by land area; celebrated alongside the Ubay-Ubay Festival. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, ubay, sto nino, january, northeast, devotional, typhoon', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-01-29'),
('ev-getafe-town-fiesta-sto-nino', 'Getafe Town Fiesta (Sto. Niño)', 'Heritage', 'Last Saturday of January', 'Last Sat Jan', 'jan', 'Getafe', '10.1500, 124.1500', 'Annual', 'Getafe''s patronal feast at a parish established in 1876 under the Augustinian Recollects, with the present church completed in 1926. Originally named ''Ambacon,'' the town was renamed after Getafe near Madrid - locally written ''Jetafe.'' The north-coast jump-off to Lapinig Island and the Danajon Bank reef.', 'Jump-off to the northern islands (Pangangan, Mahanay). Fiesta day = inflated boat fares; book ahead.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, getafe, sto nino, january, north coast, islands, devotional', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-01-01'),
('ev-dagohoy-town-fiesta-our-lady-of-lourdes', 'Dagohoy Town Fiesta (Our Lady of Lourdes)', 'Heritage', 'February 11', 'Feb 11', 'feb', 'Dagohoy', '9.9000, 124.2167', 'Annual', 'The interior town named after Francisco Dagohoy, leader of the 1744-1829 Dagohoy Revolt - the longest revolt in Philippine history. The parish was established in 1957. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, dagohoy, our lady of lourdes, february, inland, devotional, revolt', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-02-11'),
('ev-corella-town-fiesta-our-lady-of-the-village', 'Corella Town Fiesta (Our Lady of the Village)', 'Heritage', 'April 27', 'Apr 27', 'apr', 'Corella', '9.7000, 123.9167', 'Annual', 'Corella''s patronal feast for Nuestra Señora del Villar - a devotion brought from Corella in Navarra, Spain, by the Recollects. The parish was founded in 1884; the stone-church complex was completed in 1886. The present concrete church was begun in 1924. Town carved from Baclayon in 1879; home of the Philippine Tarsier Sanctuary.', 'The tarsier sanctuary closes for the fiesta procession in the afternoon. Go in the morning if it''s on your list.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, corella, our lady of the village, april, tarsier, devotional, spain', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-04-27'),
('ev-tagbilaran-city-fiesta-san-jose', 'Tagbilaran City Fiesta (San Jose)', 'Heritage', 'May 1', 'May 1', 'may', 'Tagbilaran City', '9.6471, 123.8556', 'Annual', 'Tagbilaran''s patronal feast for St. Joseph the Worker at the city cathedral - one of six original 1595 Jesuit missions in Bohol, elevated to parish in 1767 and seat of the Diocese of Tagbilaran since 1941. The Augustinian Recollects took over administration in 1768, with reconstruction running 1839-1855 and the bell tower added 1884-1888. The cathedral was proclaimed a Diocesan Shrine on May 1, 2021 and restored by the NHCP in 2020 after 2013 earthquake damage. Celebrated alongside Saulog Tagbilaran.', 'Drop into a barangay fiesta house for lunch-every household opens its doors. Bring something small if you''re hosted.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, tagbilaran, san jose, may, patron saint, cathedral, devotional, diocesan shrine', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-01'),
('ev-alburquerque-town-fiesta-sta-monica', 'Alburquerque Town Fiesta (Sta. Monica)', 'Heritage', 'May 4', 'May 4', 'may', 'Alburquerque', '9.6094, 123.9514', 'Annual', 'Alburquerque''s patronal feast for Santa Monica (mother of St. Augustine of Hippo), at a parish erected November 14, 1868 with stone-church construction begun in 1885. Famous for the unique arcaded passage connecting church and convento - not found in any other Bohol church. The complex was declared an Important Cultural Property by the National Museum in 2013. Originally a visita of Baclayon; settlement first called ''Sagunto.''', 'Pair with a Baclayon Church visit-they''re 10 minutes apart.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, alburquerque, sta monica, may, south coast, devotional, ICP, baclayon', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-04'),
('ev-mabini-town-fiesta-sta-monica', 'Mabini Town Fiesta (Sta. Monica)', 'Heritage', 'May 4', 'May 4', 'may', 'Mabini', '9.8667, 124.5167', 'Annual', 'Mabini''s patronal feast for Santa Monica. The town was formally organized in 1903 from lands previously belonging to Alicia, Cabulao, Ubay, and Candijay; the church was established in 1914 under the Augustinian Recollects, who ceded the parish to the secular clergy in 1937. The town center sits at Libas facing Cogtong Bay. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, mabini, sta monica, may, east coast, devotional, cogtong bay', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-04'),
('ev-sagbayan-town-fiesta-san-agustin-may', 'Sagbayan Town Fiesta (San Agustin - May)', 'Heritage', 'May 4', 'May 4', 'may', 'Sagbayan', '9.8917, 124.0500', 'Annual', 'The smaller of Sagbayan''s two yearly patronal feasts for St. Augustine (the August 28 fiesta draws the larger crowd). The town was created as a municipality on February 9, 1949 under President Quirino, initially named ''Borja'' after Governor Salustiano Borja. The name ''Sagbayan'' combines ''sag'' (nest) and ''bay'' (house) - ''a place for tree-houses.'' Famous today for Sagbayan Peak''s chocolate-hills viewdeck.', 'Two fiesta dates-the August one is bigger. Sagbayan Peak is a 10-min drive.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, sagbayan, san agustin, may, devotional, sagbayan peak, foundation', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-04'),
('ev-san-miguel-town-fiesta-san-miguel-arcangel', 'San Miguel Town Fiesta (San Miguel Arcangel)', 'Heritage', 'May 8', 'May 8', 'may', 'San Miguel', '9.9667, 124.2667', 'Annual', 'San Miguel''s patronal feast for St. Michael the Archangel at a parish established May 6, 1962. The town - formerly called ''Cambangay Sur'' after the Cambangay River - was created on March 14, 1961 from lands of Talibon and Trinidad. Far-inland northeast Bohol; under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, san miguel, san miguel arcangel, may, inland, devotional', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-08'),
('ev-calape-town-fiesta-san-vicente-ferrer', 'Calape Town Fiesta (San Vicente Ferrer)', 'Heritage', 'May 10', 'May 10', 'may', 'Calape', '9.8869, 123.8736', 'Annual', 'Calape''s patronal feast at a parish established in 1802 alongside the town''s founding. The present neo-Gothic church (1933-1954) was designed after Manila''s Santo Domingo Church in Intramuros by Eliseo Josol and Rosalio Real, and is widely called ''the epitome of Bohol Gothic.'' It was declared a National Cultural Treasure in May 2023 - the 9th and most recent Bohol church to receive that distinction.', 'May 10 is mid-fiesta-season chaos in central Bohol. Don''t try to combine with Tagbilaran (May 1) or Maribojoc (May 3).', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, calape, san vicente ferrer, may, west coast, devotional, national cultural treasure, gothic', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-10'),
('ev-bilar-town-fiesta-san-isidro-labrador', 'Bilar Town Fiesta (San Isidro Labrador)', 'Heritage', 'May 15', 'May 15', 'may', 'Bilar', '9.7167, 124.1083', 'Annual', 'Bilar''s patronal feast for St. Isidore the Farmer at a parish declared in 1830 (formerly a visita of Loboc). Notably, the church was occupied as a fortress by American troops during the Filipino-American War - which is why it was spared when the rest of the town was burned. Sub-territories of Bilar were later carved off to form Batuan, Carmen, and Sevilla. Most of the present church is 20th-century build.', 'Drive through the man-made forest on the way in. Fiesta-morning light through the mahogany canopy is the photo.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, bilar, san isidro labrador, may, inland, man-made forest, devotional', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-15'),
('ev-trinidad-town-fiesta-san-isidro-labrador', 'Trinidad Town Fiesta (San Isidro Labrador)', 'Heritage', 'May 15', 'May 15', 'may', 'Trinidad', '10.0833, 124.3167', 'Annual', 'Trinidad''s patronal feast for St. Isidore. The town - originally a settlement (1820) called ''Ipil'' under leader Macag - was annexed to Talibon in 1903 and restored to town status in 1947 by President Manuel Roxas, who renamed it ''Trinidad'' in honor of his First Lady. The parish became independent in 1903 after operating as a visita of Ubay from 1885. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, trinidad, san isidro labrador, may, northeast, devotional, roxas', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-15'),
('ev-tubigon-town-fiesta-san-isidro-labrador', 'Tubigon Town Fiesta (San Isidro Labrador)', 'Heritage', 'May 15', 'May 15', 'may', 'Tubigon', '9.9520, 123.9669', 'Annual', 'Tubigon''s patronal feast at a parish made independent in 1852 under the Augustinian Recollects, with the first mass in the present church held June 29, 1915. The interior murals are by Cebuano artist Raymundo Francia (1930s), and both bell tower and murals date from that era. The church was declared an Important Cultural Property in 2015 and reopened in May 2018 after 2013 earthquake restoration. Aligns with Tanda Festival.', 'Aligns with Tanda Festival window (May 6-15)-the town pulses through the whole stretch.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, tubigon, san isidro labrador, may, west coast, ferry, devotional, francia', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-15'),
('ev-candijay-town-fiesta-san-jose', 'Candijay Town Fiesta (San Jose)', 'Heritage', 'May 19', 'May 19', 'may', 'Candijay', '9.8167, 124.5167', 'Annual', 'Candijay''s patronal feast for St. Joseph at a parish erected in 1857 by the Augustinian Recollects (town established 1879). The present neo-Gothic church was built in the 20th century. The Recollects administered until 1898, returned briefly under the American period, then handed the parish over to the diocesan clergy in 1937. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, candijay, san jose, may, east coast, cogtong bay, devotional', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-19'),
('ev-san-isidro-town-fiesta-san-isidro-labrador', 'San Isidro Town Fiesta (San Isidro Labrador)', 'Heritage', 'May 29', 'May 29', 'may', 'San Isidro', '9.9119, 124.0428', 'Annual', 'San Isidro''s patronal feast for St. Isidore the Farmer - the saint that gave the town its current name. The parish was only formally established in 2015, though a chapel served the community when it was a barrio of Catigbian. Older town names include ''Macapagao'' and ''Agbunan'' (after the bugang plant whose flowers scatter in the wind). Famous for Canawa Cold Spring.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, san isidro, san isidro labrador, may, inland, devotional, canawa', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-29'),
('ev-talibon-town-fiesta-holy-trinity', 'Talibon Town Fiesta (Holy Trinity)', 'Heritage', 'Last Saturday of May (movable)', 'Last Sat May', 'may', 'Talibon', '10.1500, 124.3333', 'Annual', 'Talibon''s patronal feast at the cathedral and seat of the Diocese of Talibon, created by Pope John Paul II on January 9, 1986. The parish was founded in 1722 by the Jesuit mission; the stone church was spearheaded by the Recollects in 1852 under Fr. Lorenzo Mayor and finished in 1899. Local tradition holds that survivors from Magellan''s ship Trinidad landed in the Talibon-Getafe area after the Battle of Mactan - the origin of the Trinitarian dedication.', 'Northern Bohol''s biggest city fiesta. Talibon is also the gateway to the Danajon Bank reef.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, talibon, holy trinity, may, north coast, danajon bank, devotional, cathedral, magellan', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-05-01'),
('ev-sikatuna-town-fiesta-san-antonio-de-padua', 'Sikatuna Town Fiesta (San Antonio de Padua)', 'Heritage', 'June 13', 'Jun 13', 'jun', 'Sikatuna', '9.7167, 123.9167', 'Annual', 'Sikatuna''s patronal feast for St. Anthony of Padua at a parish established in 1935. The town is named after Datu Sikatuna, the Boholano chieftain of the 1565 Sandugo blood compact with Miguel López de Legazpi - a historic anchor that puts this small interior town at the heart of Bohol''s founding story. Under the Diocese of Tagbilaran.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, sikatuna, san antonio de padua, june, tarsier, devotional, datu sikatuna', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-06-13'),
('ev-garcia-hernandez-town-fiesta-san-juan-bautista', 'Garcia Hernandez Town Fiesta (San Juan Bautista)', 'Heritage', 'June 24', 'Jun 24', 'jun', 'Garcia Hernandez', '9.6189, 124.2389', 'Annual', 'Garcia Hernandez''s patronal feast for St. John the Baptist at a parish erected October 24, 1859 by Bishop Romualdo Jimeno of Cebu. The coral-stone church (1884-1896) is a declared Important Cultural Property of the NHCP. The town''s name is a gratitude to two Augustinian Recollect priests - José García of Loon and Narciso Hernández of Guindulman - who endorsed the petition for town status on May 27, 1854.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, garcia hernandez, san juan bautista, june, south coast, devotional, ICP', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-06-24'),
('ev-loboc-town-fiesta-san-pedro', 'Loboc Town Fiesta (San Pedro)', 'Heritage', 'June 29', 'Jun 29', 'jun', 'Loboc', '9.6383, 124.0357', 'Annual', 'Loboc''s patronal feast for St. Peter the Apostle at the second-oldest parish in Bohol - the Jesuit mission was founded in late 1596, the parish formally erected in 1602, and the present coral-stone church completed in 1734. Declared a National Cultural Treasure and National Historical Landmark, the church is also the Diocesan Shrine of Our Lady of Guadalupe in Extremadura and home to the world-renowned Loboc Children''s Choir. Significantly damaged in the 2013 earthquake.', 'The high mass at Loboc Church with the children''s choir is the moment. Get there by 8am for a seat inside.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, loboc, san pedro, june, church, choir, devotional, jesuit, national cultural treasure', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-06-29'),
('ev-inabanga-town-fiesta-san-pablo', 'Inabanga Town Fiesta (San Pablo)', 'Heritage', 'June 30', 'Jun 30', 'jun', 'Inabanga', '9.9728, 124.0631', 'Annual', 'Inabanga''s patronal feast for St. Paul the Apostle at a parish founded in 1726 by Fr. Silvestre Puigvert SJ, with the new stone church completed in 1899. The town was historic ground for the 1621-22 Tamblot Revolt area. The church was damaged repeatedly across the centuries - by Dagohoy''s followers, by American troops in 1902 (in retaliation for the Filipino attack on the Tubigon garrison), and more recently by the 2017 Maute/ISIS-linked clash. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', 'The Inabanga River fluvial procession is the highlight-starts from the church wharf around 9am.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, inabanga, san pablo, june, north coast, river, fluvial, devotional, tamblot', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-06-30'),
('ev-balilihan-town-fiesta-our-lady-of-mt-carmel', 'Balilihan Town Fiesta (Our Lady of Mt. Carmel)', 'Heritage', 'July 16', 'Jul 16', 'jul', 'Balilihan', '9.7494, 124.0428', 'Annual', 'Balilihan''s patronal feast at a parish established in 1829, founded as a Spanish-era resettlement town for ex-Dagohoy rebels returning from the mountains. The stone church was begun in 1835 under Fr. Antonio Cortes OAR and inaugurated in 1846. Famous for the Balilihan Belfry - a 3-storey square tower on Mt. Carmel Hill reached by 104 steps - declared a Philippine Historical Committee heritage structure in 1953.', 'July 16 is also Carmen''s fiesta-plan for either, not both.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, balilihan, mt carmel, july, interior, devotional, belfry, dagohoy', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-07-16'),
('ev-batuan-town-fiesta-santiago', 'Batuan Town Fiesta (Santiago)', 'Heritage', 'July 25', 'Jul 25', 'jul', 'Batuan', '9.7861, 124.1394', 'Annual', 'Batuan''s patronal feast for St. James the Greater. The church was built 1842-1864, though parish status came only in 1938 - for over a century it served as a visita of Bilar/Loboc. Cruciform plan, coral-stone facade, Baroque-colonial design. Interior murals by Boholano artist Raymundo Francia. Chocolate Hills country.', 'Quietest of the Chocolate Hills towns on fiesta day. Worth the detour if you want a fiesta without the crowd.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, batuan, santiago, july, chocolate hills, devotional, francia, baroque', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-07-25'),
('ev-alicia-town-fiesta-san-joaquin', 'Alicia Town Fiesta (San Joaquin)', 'Heritage', 'July 26', 'Jul 26', 'jul', 'Alicia', '9.8961, 124.4417', 'Annual', 'Alicia''s patronal feast for Saints Joachim and Anne - the July 26 St. Joachim feast is shared with St. Anne. The town in its present form was created on September 16, 1949 by President Quirino (EO 265) and renamed after his wife Alicia; the original settlement Batuanan, or ''Lungsod-daan,'' was a return point for ex-Dagohoy revolutionaries after 1829. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, alicia, san joaquin, sta ana, july, east coast, devotional, quirino', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-07-26'),
('ev-dauis-town-fiesta-asuncion', 'Dauis Town Fiesta (Asuncion)', 'Heritage', 'August 15', 'Aug 15', 'aug', 'Dauis', '9.6164, 123.8595', 'Annual', 'Dauis''s feast of the Assumption of Mary - the parish was established in 1697 when it separated from Baclayon, with the present church begun in 1863 and completed in 1923. The miraculous Pensive Lady of Dauis was canonically crowned in 2023. The church is a declared National Historical Landmark with a famous freshwater well inside, sitting directly under the altar. Damaged in the 2013 earthquake and restored 2015-2017.', 'The wishing well inside the church is part of the procession route. Drop a coin and read the inscriptions-they go back to the 1700s.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, dauis, asuncion, august, church, marian, devotional, pensive lady, well', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-08-15'),
('ev-panglao-town-fiesta-san-agustin', 'Panglao Town Fiesta (San Agustin)', 'Heritage', 'August 28', 'Aug 28', 'aug', 'Panglao', '9.5784, 123.7560', 'Annual', 'Panglao''s patronal feast for St. Augustine at a parish established in 1782, with the present church construction begun in 1894 and inaugurated by Bishop Juan B. Gorordo of Cebu on August 31, 1924. Notable for twin antique confessionals carved with grape-and-dove motifs and a five-storey octagonal bell-watchtower (1851) - one of the tallest of its kind in the country. The church complex, convento, watchtower, plaza, old municipio, and Escuela de Niños y Niñas are all declared Important Cultural Properties. Celebrated alongside Hudyaka sa Panglao.', 'Skip Alona Beach completely on this day. The town plaza is where the food and the community are.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, panglao, san agustin, august, church, devotional, watchtower, ICP', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-08-28'),
('ev-sagbayan-town-fiesta-san-agustin-august', 'Sagbayan Town Fiesta (San Agustin - August)', 'Heritage', 'August 28', 'Aug 28', 'aug', 'Sagbayan', '9.8917, 124.0500', 'Annual', 'Sagbayan''s larger of two yearly patronal feasts for St. Augustine (the May 4 fiesta is the smaller). The town was created in 1949 from territories of Clarin, Inabanga, Carmen, and Balilihan. Famous today for the Sagbayan Peak viewdeck of the Chocolate Hills.', 'The August fiesta is the bigger of Sagbayan''s two-Sagbayan Peak is a 10-min drive.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, sagbayan, san agustin, august, sagbayan peak, devotional', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-08-28'),
('ev-guindulman-town-fiesta-our-lady-of-consolation', 'Guindulman Town Fiesta (Our Lady of Consolation)', 'Heritage', 'September 8', 'Sep 8', 'sep', 'Guindulman', '9.7833, 124.4833', 'Annual', 'Guindulman''s patronal feast at a parish ecclesiastically separated from Jagna in 1798 - established as a resettlement town for returning Dagohoy revolutionaries. The first church was burned in an 1829 Dagohoy raid and rebuilt twice; the present coral-stone-and-wood church was finished in 1950. In 2022 the parish was granted an affinity bond with the Papal Basilica of Our Lady of Consolation in Rome.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, guindulman, our lady of consolation, september, east coast, devotional, dagohoy, papal basilica', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-09-08'),
('ev-loon-town-fiesta-birhen-sa-kasilak', 'Loon Town Fiesta (Birhen sa Kasilak)', 'Heritage', 'September 8', 'Sep 8', 'sep', 'Loon', '9.7965, 123.7964', 'Annual', 'Loon''s patronal feast for Birhen sa Kasilak (Our Lady of Light) at a parish established July 22, 1753 by the Jesuits. The present church (1855-1864), designed by Domingo de Escondrillas, was once the largest church in Bohol - it totally collapsed in the 2013 earthquake. Restoration took 8 years and reopened September 7, 2021. Declared a National Cultural Treasure (2010) and a Diocesan Shrine in 2023. Climax of the SidlaKasilak festival.', 'The fluvial procession at sunset-lit candles on bancas at Loon Bay-is the entire reason to drive here.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, loon, september, birhen sa kasilak, fluvial, marian, west coast, national cultural treasure, jesuit', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-09-08'),
('ev-dimiao-town-fiesta-san-nicolas-de-tolentino', 'Dimiao Town Fiesta (San Nicolas de Tolentino)', 'Heritage', 'September 10', 'Sep 10', 'sep', 'Dimiao', '9.6167, 124.1667', 'Annual', 'Dimiao''s patronal feast at the 6th parish founded by the Jesuits in Bohol during the Spanish era (earliest documentary mention 1750), with the present stone church built 1797-1815. Baroque architecture with notable Muslim/Moorish influence in the ornamentation. Declared a National Cultural Treasure by the National Museum in 2011. The historic Stations of the Cross chapels line the road approach.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, dimiao, san nicolas de tolentino, september, south coast, devotional, baroque, moorish, NCT', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-09-10'),
('ev-clarin-town-fiesta-san-miguel', 'Clarin Town Fiesta (San Miguel)', 'Heritage', 'September 29', 'Sep 29', 'sep', 'Clarin', '9.9572, 124.0233', 'Annual', 'Clarin''s patronal feast for St. Michael the Archangel at a parish established in 1924. The town was created in 1921 and named after Aniceto Clarin - Bohol''s first civil governor. The neo-Gothic poured-concrete church with central tower-portico, built in 1929 and remodeled in 1991, collapsed entirely in the October 15, 2013 7.2-magnitude earthquake (it had already been weakened by a 1996 quake).', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, clarin, san miguel, september, north coast, devotional, earthquake, neo-gothic', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-09-29'),
('ev-jagna-town-fiesta-san-miguel-arcangel', 'Jagna Town Fiesta (San Miguel Arcangel)', 'Heritage', 'September 29', 'Sep 29', 'sep', 'Jagna', '9.6520, 124.3633', 'Annual', 'Jagna''s patronal feast for St. Michael the Archangel at the third-oldest parish in Bohol, established by the Jesuits on September 29, 1631 as ''San Miguel de Jagna.'' The present church was built 1808-1867 after an earlier 1808 fire destroyed the original Jesuit-era three-storey church-convento. The Jesuits were replaced by Augustinian Recollects in 1768. Celebrated alongside Sinu-og Estokada.', 'Combine with a calamay stop-the town''s famous makers extend hours during fiesta week.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, jagna, san miguel, september, south coast, calamay, jesuit, third-oldest parish', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-09-29'),
('ev-buenavista-town-fiesta-rosario', 'Buenavista Town Fiesta (Rosario)', 'Heritage', 'October 7', 'Oct 7', 'oct', 'Buenavista', '10.0689, 124.1583', 'Annual', 'Buenavista''s patronal feast for Our Lady of the Most Holy Rosary at a parish made independent in 1957 (formerly a visita of Inabanga from 1874, then of Getafe). Present church is mid-20th-century with pointed-arch glass windows. Coastal town in northeastern Bohol; under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, buenavista, rosario, october, northwest coast, marian, devotional', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-10-07'),
('ev-lila-town-fiesta-rosario', 'Lila Town Fiesta (Rosario)', 'Heritage', 'October 7', 'Oct 7', 'oct', 'Lila', '9.6000, 124.1000', 'Annual', 'Lila''s patronal feast for Our Lady of the Most Holy Rosary at a parish erected July 6, 1869 with the present concrete church completed in 1925. The original light-materials church was burned by American colonizers in 1901 - the town was so devastated by the Philippine-American War that it ceased to exist until being re-established in 1915. Originally located in Macahugan, transferred to its present site in 1871.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, lila, rosario, october, south coast, marian, devotional, philippine-american war', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-10-07'),
('ev-pilar-town-fiesta-our-lady-of-the-pillar', 'Pilar Town Fiesta (Our Lady of the Pillar)', 'Heritage', 'Third Sunday of October', '3rd Sun Oct', 'oct', 'Pilar', '9.8833, 124.3667', 'Annual', 'Pilar''s patronal feast for Our Lady of the Pillar. The municipality was created on December 26, 1960 by EO 460 of President Carlos P. Garcia - formerly the barrio ''Lungsodaan'' of Sierra Bullones, which was the old seat of municipal government during Spanish times. Inland eastern Bohol; under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, pilar, our lady of pillar, october, inland east, marian, devotional, cpg', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-10-03'),
('ev-antequera-town-fiesta-rosario', 'Antequera Town Fiesta (Rosario)', 'Heritage', 'Last Saturday of October', 'Last Sat Oct', 'oct', 'Antequera', '9.7806, 123.9050', 'Annual', 'Antequera''s patronal feast for Our Lady of the Most Holy Rosary at a parish declared in 1880 under the Augustinian Recollects, with stone-church construction begun in 1896 - disrupted by the 1898 Revolution. The town was carved out of Maribojoc and Cortes in 1876. The facade features Corinthian-capitaled posts and round/arch fenestration. Damaged in the 2013 earthquake. Famous for basket weaving.', 'Fiesta day is also the best day to buy direct from basket weavers. The Sunday market doubles in size.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, antequera, rosario, october, basket weaving, marian, devotional, recollect', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-10-01'),
('ev-baclayon-town-fiesta-immaculate-conception', 'Baclayon Town Fiesta (Immaculate Conception)', 'Heritage', 'December 8', 'Dec 8', 'dec', 'Baclayon', '9.6217, 123.9120', 'Annual', 'Baclayon''s patronal feast at Bohol''s oldest Christian site - the Jesuit mission was established here on November 17, 1596 and the present coral-stone church completed in 1727. La Purísima Concepción de la Virgen María is the parish dedication. Famed for egg-white-mortar coral-stone construction; the Augustinian Recollects took over from the Jesuits in 1768. Declared a National Cultural Treasure (December 7, 2010) and National Historical Landmark. Heavily damaged in the 2013 earthquake; restored in 2017.', 'The church museum is open on fiesta day-rare access. Worth the line.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, baclayon, december, immaculate conception, marian, museum, oldest, NCT, jesuit', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-08'),
('ev-catigbian-town-fiesta-immaculate-conception', 'Catigbian Town Fiesta (Immaculate Conception)', 'Heritage', 'December 8', 'Dec 8', 'dec', 'Catigbian', '9.8333, 124.0833', 'Annual', 'Catigbian''s patronal feast at a chapel organized in 1848 under the Diocese of Cebu (mother parish: Calape). The chapel was burned by American troops on February 4, 1899 during the Filipino-American War. The town was re-established by President Quirino on June 17, 1949 - celebrated alongside the Katigbawan Festival window. Restored from 2013 earthquake damage in 2021.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, catigbian, immaculate conception, december, inland, marian, devotional, philippine-american war', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-08'),
('ev-duero-town-fiesta-immaculate-conception', 'Duero Town Fiesta (Immaculate Conception)', 'Heritage', 'December 8', 'Dec 8', 'dec', 'Duero', '9.7333, 124.4167', 'Annual', 'Duero''s patronal feast at a parish founded June 5, 1863 by the Augustinian Recollects, with the church completed in 1874. One of the very few colonial-era wooden churches in the Philippines still extant - declared a heritage site by the NHCP. Originally dedicated to St. Philomena; now to the Immaculate Conception. The Recollects left in 1898, returned in 1902, and handed the parish to the secular clergy in 1937.', 'Dec 8 Marian feast aligns with Baclayon, Catigbian, Sierra Bullones. Pick one.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, duero, immaculate conception, december, east coast, marian, wooden church, NHCP', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-08'),
('ev-sierra-bullones-town-fiesta-immaculate-conception', 'Sierra Bullones Town Fiesta (Immaculate Conception)', 'Heritage', 'December 8', 'Dec 8', 'dec', 'Sierra Bullones', '9.7833, 124.3667', 'Annual', 'Sierra Bullones''s patronal feast at a parish and town both created January 5, 1863 (previously a visita of Jagna). The town was formed by merging six interior barangays - Pamacsalan, Dinao (Bicao), Panagsagan (Guadalupe), Busoc (Bugsoc), Danicop, and Catagdaan. Striking neo-Gothic facade with quatrefoil windows and a rose-window pediment. Under the Diocese of Talibon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, sierra bullones, immaculate conception, december, inland, marian, neo-gothic, devotional', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-08'),
('ev-sevilla-town-fiesta-our-lady-of-guadalupe', 'Sevilla Town Fiesta (Our Lady of Guadalupe)', 'Heritage', 'December 12', 'Dec 12', 'dec', 'Sevilla', '9.6833, 124.0500', 'Annual', 'Sevilla''s patronal feast for Our Lady of Guadalupe of Extremadura at a parish declared October 12, 1872 (formerly a visita of Loboc). Along with Loboc and Manila''s Makati church, this is one of the three earliest Philippine sites of the Extremaduran Guadalupe devotion. The original town center at Bantig was razed by American troops in 1901; survivors crossed the Loboc River and rebuilt at present-day Maraag.', 'Right next to Loboc-pair with a river cruise lunch.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, sevilla, our lady of guadalupe, december, marian, river cruise, devotional, extremadura', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-12'),
('ev-danao-town-fiesta-holy-family', 'Danao Town Fiesta (Holy Family)', 'Heritage', 'December 30', 'Dec 30', 'dec', 'Danao', '9.8833, 124.1500', 'Annual', 'Danao''s patronal feast for the Holy Family at a parish established in 1957. Interior town under the Diocese of Talibon. Famous today for extreme adventure tourism (E.A.T. Danao zipline, Plunge) and the Francisco Dagohoy historical caves where the Boholano hero is said to have based the revolt.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, danao, holy family, december, adventure park, devotional, dagohoy caves', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-30'),
('ev-anda-town-fiesta-sto-nino', 'Anda Town Fiesta (Sto. Niño)', 'Heritage', 'Movable (Sto. Niño feast)', 'Movable', 'all', 'Anda', '9.7438, 124.5750', 'Movable', 'Anda''s patronal feast for the Holy Infant at a parish erected March 19, 1885 (royal approval January 6, 1885), with the church built 1885-1888. Famous for the 1920s ceiling murals by Cebuano artist Raymundo Francia; the bell tower was added 1950-1952. The town - formerly ''Quinali'' - was renamed after Simón de Anda y Salazar, the governor who resisted the British occupation in the 1760s.', 'Movable date-usually around the Sto. Niño feast (Jan). Check with the parish before driving 2.5 hrs east.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, anda, sto nino, movable, east coast, beach, devotional, francia, anda salazar', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-01'),
('ev-bien-unido-town-fiesta-sto-nino', 'Bien Unido Town Fiesta (Sto. Niño)', 'Heritage', 'Movable', 'Movable', 'all', 'Bien Unido', '10.1389, 124.3792', 'Movable', 'Bien Unido''s patronal feast for the Holy Child at the youngest municipality in Bohol, carved from Talibon and Trinidad on December 24, 1980 (ratified April 7, 1981). Coastal/island town under the Diocese of Talibon. Gateway to the Cabilao-area and Danajon Bank reef.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, bien unido, sto nino, movable, far north, danajon bank, devotional, youngest', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-01'),
('ev-loay-town-fiesta-holy-trinity', 'Loay Town Fiesta (Holy Trinity)', 'Heritage', 'Movable (Holy Trinity Sunday)', 'Movable', 'all', 'Loay', '9.5972, 124.0179', 'Movable', 'Loay''s patronal feast at a parish separated from Loboc in 1799 under the Augustinian Recollects. The church (1822), convent (1838), and bell tower (1865) sit on a hill facing the sea near the mouth of the Loboc River - features include a side pulpit, an 1841 pipe organ, and a tall-column choir loft. Declared a National Cultural Treasure; fully restored from 2013 earthquake damage in 2020.', 'Movable feast on Holy Trinity Sunday. Combine with Sambat Mascara (Dec) for the full Loay experience.', NULL, NULL, 'fiesta, heritage, loay, holy trinity, movable, south coast, river mouth, devotional, national cultural treasure, pipe organ', '#b1763b', 'rgba(177,118,59,0.15)', '#b1763b', 0, '2026-12-01')

